 "verdicts": {
  "A2A agents fall into two categories: client agents that initiate requests and coordinate tasks on behalf of the user, and remote/service agents that advertise specific capabilities and handle incoming requests.": 1,
  "In A2A, agents publish Agent Cards, self-descriptions of what they can do, which protocols they speak and what requests they accept, and agents exchange JSON messages over HTTP, often mediated by an A2A server.": 1,
  "MCP (Model Context Protocol), developed by Anthropic, is a structured way to let AI agents access tools, APIs, or external resources, connecting an MCP client (typically the LLM-powered agent) to local data sources and/or remote resource servers.": 1
 }
